# TYRE-21. Transitive dependencies are the exposure: 59 of 119 locked packages
# were under 14 days old before this ticket, and Renovate does not manage
# transitives at all. This gate is what stops them re-floating onto
# hours-old releases on the next resolution.
#
# Requires npm >= 11.10.0. Older npm silently ignores unknown keys, so on
# npm 10 or below this file enforces nothing at all — CI pins npm for that
# reason.
min-release-age=14

# The escape hatch for the one case where waiting is the greater risk: a
# security fix younger than the window. This mirrors, for local resolution,
# what `vulnerabilityAlerts.minimumReleaseAge: null` does for Renovate.
#
# Without this the two settings contradict each other and `npm install` dies
# with ETARGET — the package.json override pins nanoid to a version the age
# gate then refuses to resolve. `npm ci` does not re-resolve, so CI stays
# green while every fresh install fails.
#
# nanoid: GHSA-2v37-7h3g-55p8 (high, CWE-835 infinite loop). Aging the
# lockfile rolled it back to 3.3.17, which is vulnerable; 3.3.18 is the fix.
# Remove this line and the package.json override together once 3.3.18 has
# cleared 14 days on its own — after 2026-08-21.
min-release-age-exclude=nanoid
